meta {
  name: login-other-role
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{vipa}}/api/v1/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "{{otherRoleEmail}}",
    "password": "{{otherRolePassword}}"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  The same endpoint as `login`, pointed at an account that is not the administrator.

  Since US-009 every request in this collection needs a session, and what the session may
  do depends on the role it carries. Checking a folder means running it three times — as
  `admin` through `login`, then as `librarian` and as `user` through this one — and that
  is what this request exists for: switch {{otherRoleEmail}} and {{otherRolePassword}} in
  the Localhost environment instead of editing a tracked file.

  Bruno holds one cookie jar per host, so signing in here replaces the session the
  previous login opened rather than adding to it. Run `logout` between two roles if you
  want the switch to be unambiguous; run `csrf` after either one, since both replace the
  token.

  The account needs a row in `auth_identity` with a `local` password hash, and the dev
  fixtures create none — see the notes in `login`. Both the address and the password come
  from the environment: a student's real address has no place in the repository.

  What the answer tells you is the role: the 200 body carries it, and it is the value the
  matrix in the folder docs is read against.
}
